Added measures of association for nominal data to contingency stats module. Measures added include Pearsons Contingency Coefficient, Tschuprow's T, Cramer's V and Phi. Measures are individual specified by values of the 'stat' argument (as 'C', 'T', 'V' or 'phi', respectively) within function scipy.stats.contingency.association_test.

These measures can provide useful information about variable independence to those performing chi-squared tests or categorical data analysis in general. Each of the measures is empirically estimated using the chi-squared statistic and are valid for 2d arrays. 


